    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!--      2026-09-15: BL0016 is not an error in THIS project, and nowhere else.

      Directory.Build.props sets TreatWarningsAsErrors=true, and its safety valve
      (CodeAnalysisTreatWarningsAsErrors=false) exempts CA rules only. BL0016 is a Blazor SDK rule,
      so the valve misses it and every hit became a build error: 28 of them, all in this project,
      failing the phase-4 gate and with it the required `verify` check on every platform pull
      request. main's own validate had been red on this since 2026-09-13.

      BL0016 asks that a JS interop call be guarded with try/catch, because a component whose
      circuit has disconnected throws. That is sound advice for a COMPONENT. These are bUnit tests
      that invoke interop deliberately, and a try/catch around them would swallow the exact failure
      each test exists to detect — the guard would make the test unable to fail.

      WarningsNotAsErrors, not NoWarn: the rule still runs and each hit is still emitted, counted
      and visible in the build log, exactly as the CA wave is. The production Blazor projects keep
      BL0016 binding as an error; nothing here changes them.
    -->
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>$(WarningsNotAsErrors);BL0016</WarningsNotAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
